# Raw third-party datasets (~140 MB) stay out of git, but their provenance
# note must not — it records the data-integrity findings that constrain how
# every derived feature may present its numbers. Ignore the contents, not the
# directory, so the negation below can take effect.
datasets/*
!datasets/README.md

docs/

# Python virtualenv for the ML training phase. The backend is Node; this venv
# exists only for ml/ and is created with --system-site-packages so torch and
# pandas come from the global install rather than being duplicated.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Trained model artifacts. These are build outputs of `ml/training/*`, are
# large binaries, and are reproducible from the pinned versions in
# ml/requirements.txt plus the raw CSVs. Their measured metrics live in
# ml/MODEL_RESULTS.md, which IS tracked — that is the reviewable artifact.
ml/artifacts/
